\subsection{Dimensionality of the School Climate Questionnaire}<<CMD_660>>

We explored the dimensions of the item responses with a principle component analysis (PCA) of the correlation matrix. We applied the PCA to the data from all schools. Although a multigroup factor model or a multilevel factor model may be more appropriate, we considered a PCA as sufficient for an exploratory analysis, given that the inter-school differences were rather small (see the supplementary materials for a comparison of 4 schools). The eigen values showed that there might be <<MATH_INLINE_145>> or <<MATH_INLINE_146>> components. The eigen values were <<MATH_INLINE_147>> <<MATH_INLINE_148>>  <<MATH_INLINE_149>> <<MATH_INLINE_150>>, and <<MATH_INLINE_151>> <<MATH_INLINE_152>> for the first four components, respectively. 

